ven Spielberg's DreamWorks  studio that was one problem though  Spielberg didn't like the original  ending which showed Katy being shot by  police instead he came up with the idea  for the ending you saw in the theaters  with Katie's demonic face seared into  your retinas forever so you can blame  your nightmares on Spielberg paranormal  reactivity when DreamWorks picked up the  film the plan was to remake it with  bigger stars and bigger budget but as  part of the contract the Los Angeles  Times reports pally and producer Jason  Blum required the studio to hold at  least one test screening of the original  cut before pulling the trigger on the  remake to see if audiences liked it when  viewers at the test screening started  walking out of the theater midway  through the film it looked bad with  studio exec Adam Goodman calling it one  of the worst previews he'd ever been a  part of until the exit interviews showed  the attendees were leaving because they  were too terrified to keep watching it  just like that a hit was born infectious  belly was clearly inspired by the Blair  Witch Project not just in terms of style  and budget but also viral marketing case  in point  he kept the stars katie featherston and  mika slope hidden away in the hopes that  it might help generate some extra  mystery Pelle told the Los Angeles Times  he made the decision because the less  people know about paranormal activity  the more they enjoy it I don't think  there's anything to be gained by putting  the filmmakers and the cast in front so  much money it's scary  if you thought demonic possession was  frightening  here's something even more terrifying  math  with a worldwide return of 193 million  dollars Paranormal Activity boasts an  absurd 1.28 million percent return on  its initial $15,000 budget that profit  margin is more than double the return  earned by the second most profitable  film ever which was that's right the  Blair Witch Project time to get your  GoPro go downstairs and make some back  come on haunting Steven Spielberg is  responsible for some of the biggest  scares ever thanks to jaws but even he  was terrified by paranormal activity  thanks in part to a supernatural  experience he had while screening the  DVD somehow his bedroom door wound up  locked from the inside  that coupled with the freakiness of the  movie weak doubt the legendary director  so much that he put the DVD in a trash  bag when he returned it the next day so  he wouldn't have to physically touch it  surprising he didn't just feed it to the  Sharks  Japanese spin-off Paranormal Activity  has spawned half-a-dozen follow-ups and  spin-offs but there's one that stands  out as a curious black sheep among the  franchise Tokyo Knight around the same  time Paranormal Activity 2 was being put  together for us release the studio  license to the franchise out for a  parallel sequel for release in Japan  which follows a Japanese student who  brings the spirit back to Tokyo  following a trip to San Diego  sorry Japan thanks for watching  subscribe to our YouTube channel to  watch more videos like the one you just  saw and leave us a comment to let us  know what scared you the most about  paranormal activity
 

